## Top face and gauges

Top-face policy:

```text
u'=1:  fixed y^V2'(y-x)
u'=2:  fixed y^V2'(y^2-x^2)
u'>=3: not licensed for new rows here; run/count D1-only with monic y^K fixed
```

The only u'>=3 fixed-top exception is the Moh/Appendix-II control
`(15,10;11;2;k=2)`, where the charged compiler licenses the printed
`y^2(y-x)^3` control and requires `[1]`.  For all new u'>=3 rows, a fixed
`y^V(y-x)^u` kill would be a slice, so it is not used as a theorem.

K16 rows use the generalized Theorem-1.2 flag basis derived from the independent
t=2 generator:

```text
h = y A + b4,  A = y B + b3,  B = y(y-x) + b1 y + b2.
```

For a K16 row, the target shear gauge is applied only when the driver verifies
that `alpha_(e'-d')` is scalar and every shifted beta basis lies inside the
corresponding alpha filtration.  The applied gauges were:

```text
(16,12): P -> P - alpha_1 Q; Q const(beta_3); P const(alpha_4)
(28,20): P -> P - alpha_2 Q; Q const(beta_5); P const(alpha_7)
(40,28): P -> P - alpha_3 Q; Q const(beta_7); P const(alpha_10)
```

No target gauge is applied to the d'=2,e'=3 A/B systems.

